From acfe4eec917f7d5b2c0d9754fbae27f2f2b68c5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Augustya Baghel <261733204+astytimestwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:10:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linux-samsung-beyond1lte-downstream: kernel v2 for server use

Config:
- SND_ALOOP=y: ALSA loopback card, so a DSP (CamillaDSP) can sit between
  players and a USB sound card.
- LOD_SEC off: Samsung's "Linux on DeX" hardening refuses user namespaces
  for non-root ("LOD: blocking USERNS from non-root"); off = mainline behaviour.
- OVERLAY_FS=y, NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_MULTIPORT=y, FHANDLE=y, USB_NET_RNDIS_HOST=y.
- NF_TABLES stays off on purpose: with unprivileged user namespaces it is a
  known local-root surface on a 4.14 kernel, and nothing here needs it.

tzdev-idle-waits.patch: the TEE kernel threads (tz_worker_thread x8,
tz_iwsock, ree_time, scsi_srpmb_worker) slept in TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE, which
counts as load, so an idle phone showed a load average of ~11. They now sleep
in TASK_IDLE (same semantics, like wait_event_idle() in Linux 4.17+).
Result on the device: 0 tasks in D state, load average ~0.3 when idle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
